11-03 09:37:13.191  8940  8961 D LiteRtRepository: Return only compact JSON {"score":N,"missing_points":[],"followup_needed":false}. N must be an integer 1-100 for relevance, completeness and accuracy against the original target. Evaluate the original answer and all answered followup pairs together. Before emitting JSON, compare every candidate missing point against the original answer and every answered follow-up pair. If an answered follow-up directly supplies that information, do not include it in missing_points. Recompute score, missing_points, and followup_needed together as one consistent final decision. Treat each independently answerable required component as a separate missing_points item; never combine independently answerable deficiencies. After every answered follow-up, recompute components independently and omit each supplied component even when another component from the same target remains missing. When a Required component catalog is present, evaluate each catalog item independently: missing_points may contain only configured component IDs. Omit IDs whose component is supplied by the original answer or answered follow-up pairs; never return component descriptions or questions as missing_points. When a Required components block is present, missing_points may contain only the exact text of unresolved configured components. Separate relevance from completeness. An answer can discuss the right topic but still be incomplete. Score 90-100 only when the respondent explicitly provides every material component requested by the Expected answer target and Question. Do not infer missing details from general knowledge, plausibility, or a bare statement that an event occurred. A concise answer may be complete. A verbose or relevant answer that omits any material requested component must score below 90. For example, saying that an event occurred without describing its requested effect is incomplete. Consistency rule: if missing_points is non-empty or followup_needed is true, score must be an integer from 1 to 89. Scores 90-100 are allowed only when missing_points=[] and followup_needed=false. Never use score 90 as a borderline value when anything is missing. For any score below 90, missing_points must contain the specific missing or ambiguous target-required information and followup_needed must be true. Otherwise missing_points is empty and followup_needed is false. Do not generate a question. Do not penalize style or request information outside the target. Write missing_points in English.
